# Level 3 → Level 4

## Concept
This level hides the password in a file inside a hidden directory 
(`inhere`), with a filename designed to trip you up — it starts with 
three literal dots, which looks almost identical to the `.` and `..` 
entries `ls -a` always shows, so it's easy to overlook or mistype.

## Commands used
cat "./...Hiding-From-You"

## Why it works
The quotes tell the shell to treat the whole filename as one exact 
string, dots and all, instead of trying to interpret any part of it 
differently. The `./` explicitly points at the current directory, 
which removes any ambiguity about where the file lives — useful 
since the name itself already looks confusing at a glance.
